    {
        "content": "<p><a href=\"https://github.com/lunsong/JaxProof\">This</a> is an ongoing project to generate and verify Jax code. Now you can write neural networks in Lean<br>\n<a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/Ao-kXNQLyAtT2Gm04J1Flh8J/Screenshot-from-2025-12-28-18-50-47.png\">Screenshot from 2025-12-28 18-50-47.png</a></p>\n<div class=\"message_inline_image\"><a href=\"/user_uploads/3121/Ao-kXNQLyAtT2Gm04J1Flh8J/Screenshot-from-2025-12-28-18-50-47.png\" title=\"Screenshot from 2025-12-28 18-50-47.png\"><img data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1920x1200\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/3121/Ao-kXNQLyAtT2Gm04J1Flh8J/Screenshot-from-2025-12-28-18-50-47.png/840x560.webp\"></a></div>",
        "id": 565562330,
        "sender_full_name": "Lun Song",
        "timestamp": 1766920055
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Very cool! How does this handle the opaqueness of <code>Float</code> operations?</p>",
        "id": 565582740,
        "sender_full_name": "Alex Meiburg",
        "timestamp": 1766945525
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Currently I treat float numbers as real numbers, but it can be extended to other approximations like treating float numbers as random variables. The defined jax functions are actually  function templates which rely on a typeclass <code>Jax.Impl</code>, which I have defined two instances ,<code>Jax.Tracer</code> to generate  code, and <code>Jax.Array</code> to prove properties assuming float is real. To support other approximations or backends, we can simply define a new <code>Jax.Impl</code> instance</p>",
        "id": 565612343,
        "sender_full_name": "Lun Song",
        "timestamp": 1766982544
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Updates: I have recently made major changes to this project, now the DSL looks like (full example can be found in the repo)</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">JaxProof</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">xla</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">returns</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">begin</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">let_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">choice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">let_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cumsum</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">let_expr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">choice</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x_id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x_id</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IO</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">println</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">pretty_print</span>\n<span class=\"c\">/-</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  %0: const int [12] 1</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  %1: const int [12] 0</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  %2: where $0 %0 %1</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  %3: cumsum %2</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  %4: where %2 %3 %1</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  return %4,</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">-/</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">List</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">idxOf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Finset</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero_eq_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Jax</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">FloatAsReal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">idxOfNonzero_def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 581813053,
        "sender_full_name": "Lun Song",
        "timestamp": 1774505542
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Updates: I have added support for more primitives, implemented a python backend for evaluation. I have also added more examples, including implementing the <a href=\"https://github.com/lunsong/JaxProof/blob/master/Tests/SchNet.lean\">SchNet</a> and proving its permutation equivariance.</p>",
